1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:01,990
Drop Saturn in your bath.

2
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:02,960
Sink...

3
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,054
or float?

4
00:00:04,054 --> 00:00:05,180
It FLOATS!

5
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:06,721
Like a giant...

6
00:00:06,721 --> 00:00:07,800
rubber duck.

7
00:00:07,843 --> 00:00:09,540
Scoop out a cup of Saturn...

8
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:10,433
it's LIGHTER

9
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:11,833
than a cup of water.

10
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:13,610
Because Saturn's not rock.

11
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:15,433
It's mostly GAS.

12
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:16,470
Earth?

13
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:17,450
Sinks.

14
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,393
Jupiter?

15
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:19,150
Sinks.

16
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:20,690
Of all our planets...

17
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:22,467
only SATURN floats.

18
00:00:22,510 --> 00:00:23,250
Catch?

19
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:24,778
It'd probably fall apart.

20
00:00:24,778 --> 00:00:25,933
The core sinks...

21
00:00:25,981 --> 00:00:27,800
the gas fizzes UP.

22
00:00:27,842 --> 00:00:29,330
And its icy rings?

23
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:30,467
They float.

24
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,647
So yes...

25
00:00:31,647 --> 00:00:33,567
it leaves a RING.

